# Note: Existing status codes, redirect targets, JSON bodies and render behavior are
# unchanged. The Auth.js `auth()` middleware wrapper rebuilds the Response
# (`new Response(body, response)`); the tested 307/401/403/200 branches all keep the
# header because the outer proxy layer attaches it after the wrapper returns.

## Inbound validation and generated IDs
# - valid 8-64 char [A-Za-z0-9._-] value preserved: matrix-request-0001
# - overlong / too-short values replaced by a 36-char UUID
# - missing values replaced by crypto.randomUUID()

## Correlation sample: response header == service log == route log
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-11-10T16:46:28.556Z","level":"info","event":"http.health.check","service":"flower-wms","env":"development","version":"unknown","requestId":"matrix-request-0001","fields":{"outcome":"success","status":200,"v1DurationMs":2,"v2DurationMs":2}}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-11-10T16:46:28.556Z","level":"info","event":"http.request","service":"flower-wms","env":"development","version":"unknown","requestId":"matrix-request-0001","fields":{"method":"GET","route":"/api/health","status":200,"durationMs":2}}
CASE health-inbound-valid | status=200 | requestId=matrix-request-0001 | body={"status":"ok"}

## Concurrency (no cross-request ID bleed)
CONCURRENCY_INBOUND count=20 unique=20 allMatch=true
CONCURRENCY_GENERATED count=20 unique=20
# Each of 20 concurrent requests with a distinct inbound ID got its own ID back, and the
# 20 requests without an inbound ID received 20 distinct UUIDs. Route logs for the same
# requests also carry their own IDs (e.g. requestId=concurrent-request-0000 ... 0019).

## Instrumentation
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-11-10T16:46:24.085Z","level":"info","event":"service.started","service":"flower-wms","env":"development","version":"unknown","fields":{"pid":11540,"nodeEnv":"development"}}
# register() ran once per server instance; no Edge-runtime Node API warning after the pid read
# moved behind a globalThis accessor (the Node-only branch still reports the real pid).

## Matcher coverage (allow-list; static assets are never matched)
# covered:      /, /login, /v2(/*), /wms/*, /cms/*, /admin/*,
#               /api/admin/*, /api/cms/*, /api/business/*, /api/health (added by E3.2)
# not covered:  /api/auth/* (Auth.js callbacks), /api/miniprogram/*, /uploads/*,
#               /_next/static, /_next/image, /favicon.ico
# Adding /api/auth/* was intentionally avoided (Auth.js callback behavior must not change).
# A 302 response from the Auth.js callback therefore carries no proxy request ID; this is
# documented as a known boundary, not a regression.

